<!-- SLIDE 1 -->
<div class="slide" align="center">
<br><br><br>
<h1>CarbonSathi</h1>
<p class="big">AI-powered carbon accounting &amp; compliance assistant for India's MSMEs</p>
<p style="font-size:16pt">Photograph a bill. Know your emissions. Keep your buyers.</p>
<br><br>
<p style="font-size:14pt"><b>Gaurav Barhate</b> · B.Tech CSE, IIIT Vadodara (2026)<br>
Ideas of India – Season 2 · Sustainable &amp; Resilient India · Climate Tech &amp; Carbon Management<br>
Concept-to-Prototype Execution Plan</p>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 2 -->
<div class="slide">
<h2>The problem arrived with two deadlines</h2>
<br>
<p><span class="stat">31 July 2026</span> — India's first CCTS carbon-compliance filings fall due. ~490 plants in 7 sectors already carry binding targets; penalty is 2× the carbon-credit price.</p>
<p><span class="stat">1 January 2026</span> — EU's CBAM entered its paid phase. €8–9 billion of Indian exports now carry a carbon cost (GTRI: 15–22% effective price pressure on coal-based steel &amp; aluminium).</p>
<p><span class="stat">8.7 crore MSMEs</span> — 31.1% of GDP, 48.6% of exports, 38.9 crore jobs — and almost none of them can measure their own carbon footprint. Their buyers are starting to ask.</p>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 3 -->
<div class="slide">
<h2>Who suffers: the owner with no sustainability team</h2>
<br>
<p class="big">A tile maker in Morbi. A dyeing unit owner in Tiruppur.</p>
<ul>
<li>Records = paper bills + photos on a phone + WhatsApp</li>
<li>Consultants cost more than his yearly paperwork budget; enterprise carbon software is English-only, corporate-priced, months to deploy</li>
<li>His buyer just asked for emissions data. He has no way to answer.</li>
</ul>
<div class="box"><b>The gap:</b> no tool combines AI document reading + Indian languages + India-specific factors + compliance outputs + an MSME price. That empty quadrant is CarbonSathi.</div>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 4 -->
<div class="slide">
<h2>The solution: 4 steps, minutes not weeks</h2>
<br>
<table>
<tr><th width="12%">Step</th><th>What happens</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>1. Upload</b></td><td>Owner photographs electricity bills / fuel invoices — any format, any language</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>2. AI reads</b></td><td>LLM + OCR extraction turns documents into structured consumption data</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>3. Compute</b></td><td>India-native factor engine (CEA grid factor 0.7117 tCO₂/MWh v21.0, IPCC, India GHG Program) → Scope 1, 2, 3 emissions</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>4. Act</b></td><td>Live dashboard · CCTS-Form-A-style &amp; CBAM/buyer-ready reports · savings actions ranked by payback · water &amp; material-waste tracking · credit-readiness score</td></tr>
</table>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 5 -->
<div class="slide">
<h2>Architecture (built on a proven stack)</h2>
<br>
<div class="box" style="font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13pt">
[Mobile / Web — vernacular UI]<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;↓ upload (photo/PDF)<br>
[AI Extraction Engine — LLM + OCR] → structured energy &amp; material data<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
[Emission-Factor Core — CEA · IPCC · BEE · India GHG Program (config-driven)]<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
[GHG Ledger — Scope 1 / 2 / 3] → [Reports: CCTS-style · CBAM · buyer]<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
[Recommendation Engine — savings ranked by payback · credit-readiness score]
</div>
<p>Stack: React · Node.js/Express · MongoDB · Redis/BullMQ queues · Socket.IO real-time · JWT/OAuth · Docker/CI-CD. Stateless and queue-based, so it scales horizontally.</p>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 6 -->
<div class="slide">
<h2>Status: functional prototype, honestly stated</h2>
<br>
<p class="big">Working today</p>
<ul>
<li>End-to-end flow runs: upload → AI extraction → CO₂e calculation → dashboard → PDF report mirroring CCTS Form-A fields</li>
<li>Factor outputs cross-checked against published CEA/BEE values; tested on simulated datasets for two unit archetypes (ceramic kiln, textile dyeing)</li>
</ul>
<p class="big">Not yet done</p>
<ul>
<li>Live commercial pilot · verifier (ACVA) integration · full language coverage</li>
</ul>
<div class="box"><b>Execution credibility:</b> applicant has shipped two production platforms on this stack — a real-time collaborative coding/interview platform with AI evaluation, and a fault-tolerant webhook security service (zero payload loss under concurrent load).</div>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 7 -->
<div class="slide">
<h2>Why nothing else fills this gap</h2>
<br>
<table>
<tr><th></th><th>Enterprise (Persefoni, Watershed, Sweep)</th><th>Indian ESG tools (sentra.world, Greenio, Zoei)</th><th>IIM-B free tool</th><th>Consultants</th><th><b>CarbonSathi</b></th></tr>
<tr><td><b>MSME price</b></td><td>No</td><td>Partly</td><td>Free</td><td>No</td><td><b>₹500–2,000/mo</b></td></tr>
<tr><td><b>AI reads documents</b></td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>No (manual entry)</td><td>Human</td><td><b>Yes</b></td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Indian languages</b></td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Sometimes</td><td><b>10+ planned</b></td></tr>
<tr><td><b>CCTS/CBAM outputs</b></td><td>No</td><td>Partial</td><td>No</td><td>Yes, costly</td><td><b>Yes, native</b></td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Serves lakhs of units</b></td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td><b>Yes — software scales</b></td></tr>
</table>
<p>Result: ~100× cheaper than the consultant route; measurement drops from weeks to minutes.</p>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 8 -->
<div class="slide">
<h2>Year-1 pilot targets (conservative, sourced)</h2>
<br>
<table>
<tr><th>Outcome</th><th>Target</th><th>Basis</th></tr>
